### FilmFuse core-api - profile photo
# Token: see me.http. Flow: 1) get a signed upload URL, 2) PUT the JPEG to it, 3) confirm the path.
# With SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY blank, core-api uses a mock storage gateway: step 1 returns a fake
# URL (step 2 will fail) but steps 1 and 3 still exercise the API. For a real upload against
# `supabase start`, set the service_role key that `supabase status` prints.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@token = paste-access-token-here

### 1) Signed upload URL -> {uploadUrl, path: "<userId>/<uuid>.jpg", expiresInSeconds}
# @name uploadUrl
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/profile-photo/upload-url
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2) Upload the JPEG straight to Supabase Storage (no FilmFuse token; max 2 MB, image/jpeg only)
PUT {{uploadUrl.response.body.uploadUrl}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./sample.jpg

### 3) Confirm -> profile with profileImageUrl = public URL (the previous photo is deleted)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/profile-photo
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "path": "{{uploadUrl.response.body.path}}"
}

### Someone else's folder (or anything not <yourId>/<uuid>.jpg) -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/profile-photo
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "path": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111.jpg"
}

### Remove the photo -> profile with profileImageUrl null
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me/profile-photo
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
